        <div class="bignum">3<sup>+</sup></div>
        <div>
          <span class="label">Challenge</span>
          <p class="challenge-body">Singapore has high banking penetration — users hold 3+ banking relationships on average. Incumbents lock users in with Total Relationship Banking and Priority Banking, and since banking products look alike, switching a primary account is costly.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="sub-p"><b>Our wedge:</b> experience is our main competitive edge — simplicity and clarity. Value propositions:</p>
      <div class="values">
        <div class="value-card"><h4>Unconditional savings account</h4><p>No salary credit required, no minimum balance.</p></div>
        <div class="value-card"><h4>No-frills credit card</h4><p>Easy-to-calculate cashback, no cap, no minimum spend.</p></div>
        <div class="value-card"><h4>Investing products</h4><p>The lowest fees in the industry.</p></div>
      </div>

      <h3 class="sub-h"><span class="no">1</span>From secondary to primary bank</h3>
      <p class="sub-p">MariBank's current position is a user's secondary bank; the long-term goal is to become the primary bank for young users. We break that into three stages, each with its own experience milestones.</p>
      <div class="stages">
        {mariBankStages.map((s, i) => (
